auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # m-Seismo API

  Run against the dev stack (`make dev-up`) or any deployment: set `baseUrl`
  and `baseUrlRoot` in an environment (see `environments/local.bru`).

  Every request and response body is JSON. Collection-level auth is a
  bearer token from the `token` variable, filled in automatically by
  **Auth and owners / Register** or **Login** (their `vars:post-response`
  script sets it). Requests that don't need it (register, login, the
  provider callback, health) override auth to `none`.

  Folders follow backend/docs/*.md: run **Auth and owners → Register**
  first, then **Apps → Create App** and **Projects → Create Project** to
  fill in `appId` / `projectId` used by the rest of the collection.

  Errors are always `{"error": "..."}`. See backend/docs/gitlab-bitbucket.md
  and backend/docs/github.md for the full status-code and failure-mode
  reference; this collection documents request shape, not every edge case.
}
